  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Say Yes to Youth!</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young people globally continue to make up a large percentage of the population. In Africa, the number of young people under the ageof 35 years reaches almost 1 billion; representing 22.7% of the world&apos;s total population. Unfortunately, they experience some of the poorest reproductive health outcomes and are accorded the fewest opportunities in participating in spaces where decisions are madeabout their bodies.

As we enter 2025, young people worldwide continue to fight for their right to make decisions about their own bodies. Despite their strong willingness and capability to engage in policies and processes surrounding their sexual and reproductivehealth and rights (SRHR) young people and youth organisations still remain underrepresented. Young people lack the spaces and structures they need to meaningfully contribute to the development, implementation and follow up of SRHR policies, meaning that decisionsmade about their own bodies do not reflect their realities.

This project, led by CHOICE for Youth and Sexuality and the SRHR Alliance Kenya, seeks to break down these barriers and create clear pathways for young people to become effective advocates for their SRHR. Both CHOICE and SRHR Alliance have a strong track record in creating inclusive spaces for young people to advocate for their SRHR, and in facilitating their engagement in advocacy spaces. Through a cross-continental learning exchange, this initiative will use online workshops, peer educators and stories of change to engage more youngpeople in youth-led SRHR advocacy. By empowering young people with knowledge and skills, this project will ensure they can actively participate in shaping policies that affect their lives.</narrative>
  </description>
